{"meta":{"ticker":"VOOV","as_of_date":"2026-08-19","performance_as_of":"2026-07-31","generated_at":"2026-08-20 11:22:20"},"benchmark":{"ticker":"SPY","fund_name":"State Street SPDR S&P 500 ETF"},"overview":{"ticker":"VOOV","fund_name":"Vanguard S&P 500 Value ETF","category":"US Large-Cap Value","issuer":"Vanguard","index_name":"S&P 500 Value","region":"North America","exchange":"NYSEARCA","expense_ratio":0.0007,"aum":6767281400,"holdings_count":456,"inception_date":"2010-09-07","overall_score":7.07904199646643,"overall_rank":310,"sector_diversification_score":7.56019603880355},"description":{"tsi_description":"VOOV is a passive large-cap value ETF that tracks the S&P 500 Value Index and emphasizes companies with attractive valuation characteristics relative to their growth profiles. The fund uses a multi-factor style classification process that evaluates both value and growth characteristics, resulting in occasional exposure to growth-oriented stocks experiencing weaker price momentum. Unlike more concentrated or actively managed value ETFs, VOOV maintains broad diversification across all major sectors and tends to deliver relatively consistent category-relative performance over time. Its lower portfolio beta and balanced sector allocations have historically helped reduce downside risk compared to growth-focused peers. Overall, VOOV offers a diversified and relatively conservative approach to large-cap value investing.","strategy_steps":["Tracks the S&P 500 Value Index.","Starts with companies in the S&P 500 Index.","Assigns both value and growth scores to all eligible securities.","Evaluates value characteristics using book-to-price, earnings-to-price, and sales-to-price ratios.","Evaluates growth characteristics using three-year earnings growth, three-year sales growth, and twelve-month price momentum.","Classifies stocks based on combined value and growth factor scores.","Uses market-capitalization weighting after style classification.","Allows certain stocks to 